# are collinear and the two ends lie on opposite sides of it: for P = (a, b),
# Q = (c, d), R = (e, f), (R - Q)/(P - Q) is a negative real just where
# (a - c)(f - d) = (e - c)(b - d) and the dot product
# (a - c)(e - c) + (b - d)(f - d) is negative.
