# The equality case of the triangle inequality. Where |x| + |y| = |y - x|,
# squaring gives |x| |y| = -Re(y conj(x)) (`galgsq`); the absolute value of
# y conj(x) is |x| |y|, so -(y conj(x)) has real part equal to its absolute
# value, hence imaginary part 0 (`gretoim`), and y conj(x) is a negative
# real: y/x is a negative real (`gdivneg`), which is Q between P and R.
